# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream checkout, not ours to commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# robocasa/ is a shallow clone of github.com/robocasa/robocasa, ~81 MB with its
# own .git inside. A nested repository cannot be committed as ordinary files,
# and it is only needed once, to build assets/products/. See the README.
robocasa/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# out/scene.xml and out/bench.xml ARE committed. They are generated, but the
# generator is seeded so they are byte-identical run to run, they are small
# (192 kB and 2 kB), and because assets/products/ is committed too they open in
# any MuJoCo viewer straight from a clone. Committing them also makes scene
# changes show up as a reviewable diff. Regenerate after touching scene.py.
#
# Depth arrays are large and rebuildable from any scene.
out/**/*.npy
# Scratch renders. docs/figures/ holds the curated ones.
out/shots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs, editors, OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# teleop
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session recordings (--record) and the frames beside them. These contain
# webcam footage of whoever was operating, so they are not only large but
# personal; they are diagnostic scratch, never inputs to anything.
out/session*
out/rec_*
out/teleop_*.png
# MediaPipe model bundles, ~23 MB, re-downloaded on first run by tracking.py.
teleop/models/*.task
